															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stormbreath" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3075960); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3075960&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606447315" alt="stormbreath" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3075960)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stormbreath" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3075960); return false;" >stormbreath</a></span> <span class="odate time_1511387151 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2017 21:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3637829">
									

<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Did the world end that morning?&quot;<br />
&quot;I'm not really sure.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>First format screw, although there is a perfectly normal SCP buried in there.</p>
<p>At one point, this was intended as an entry for the 2015 <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-1271813">Tag-Less</a> Challenge. It only gets 10 points there, because it does have three additional tags, but the object class tag is unclassed to make up for that. This wasn't originally made for that, but then I found out about it and decided to shift it up to make it work. (If I <em>really</em> wanted, I probably could have made this a generic warping event, not necessarily a CK)</p>
<p>The one big thing I had to change was a list of GoI responses I had included at one point. I've included them below (as a note, they're all meant to be canon to the article). Now that it's gotten tagged with a couple tags, I could add these back, but I think the article works better the way it is right now.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;GoI&nbsp;Responses</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Other GoI's that monitor the integrity of reality have been reached as to whether or not they also experienced a similar event at 0427 UTC, 18/03/2016. All that have responded have indicated their detectors also malfunctioned:<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-922961-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-922961-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Global Occult Coalition:</strong> &quot;&#8230; while we will not elaborate on the methods we used to determine if such an event took place, we can confirm that we detected an event such as you have described &#8230;&quot;</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Unidentified Incidents Unit:</strong> &quot;&#8230; PatternSweep detected <tt>Positive</tt> at 11:27 EST 03/17/2016, and the matter is currently under active investigation &#8230; &quot;</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Marshall, Carter and Dark:</strong> &quot;&#8230; Every single one of our anomalous tripwires was malfunctioned at 0427 UTC, 18/03/2016. This constitutes a massive loss of profit, exceeding $5,000,000&#8230;&quot;</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>ORIA:</strong> &quot;&#8230; We have reason to believe that the events of 7:57 AM, 18 March 2016 represent widespread anomalous influence of unknown&#8230;&quot;</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Horizon Initiative:</strong> &quot;&#8230;several of our artifacts detected a notable shift in Hume and Akiva levels at the indicated time&#8230;&quot;<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-922961-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-922961-2')">2</a></sup></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Swiss Government:</strong> &quot;&#8230; our anomaly-detection system has indicated that 0527 Zurich Time should have a rating of <tt>Leuthari II/Mederich</tt>, indicating an absolute certainty of anomaly&#8230;&quot;</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/leveritas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1558990); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1558990&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1524107032" alt="Leveritas" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1558990)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/leveritas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1558990); return false;">Leveritas</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drchandra" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1956625); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1956625&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1524107032" alt="DrChandra" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1956625)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drchandra" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1956625); return false;">DrChandra</a></span> for looking this over in draft form.</p>
<hr />
<p>If you liked this thing and would like to read some comments about it, or check out other things I've written, head to <a href="/stormbreath">my author page</a> for more!</p>
